Somehow he knew about specifically that libcdt-4.dll was missing. I am  
just wondering how.

We do know that libcdt-4.dll has been renamed. Unfortunately  
libgraph-5.dll has been renamed to libgraph.dll conflicting with the  
Bioconductor package graph, but that has been fixed by Patrick.

It has always been essential that Rgraphviz is used with the same  
version it was build with. I have tried to do somediagnosis of this  
when loading Rgraphviz, but unfortunately (at least on windows), in  
this case (since it is not just a version conflict, but also a case of  
renamed dlls), it bangs out with an error before checks can be run.

This might be fixable, but I will need a some way to test it on  
windows. Guess I need to look into getting a virtual machine. Have  
anyone tried running/building R under Fusion or Parallels on the Mac?

Kasper

